IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `aa-estates`
IMPORT `aa-qa`

-- Administration Act 1903 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (aa-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for every role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error
-- ("it is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value
-- that makes the situation not hold and every later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the family
-- member and the executor (the baseline's seat) the answer is also asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer
-- on the same facts. For the beneficiary and the creditor the answers are worked by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts: the WA lives' families (Sue in 2060, two children; Jake in 2079, Ruby alone) and the baseline's worked
-- families, with the baseline's encoder's dollar figures. Expected values are written by hand from the deposited text,
-- never copied from the output. The mechanical cases at the end are generated by the scratchpad script gen_aa.py from
-- the layer's own @export list.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked rate` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked estate` IS A `What the person who died left`
ASSUME `an unasked place` IS A `My place in the family`
ASSUME `an unasked family` IS A `The family left behind`
ASSUME `unasked sums` IS A `Legacy sums`
ASSUME `an unasked home` IS A `The home`
ASSUME `an unasked relation` IS A `My relation to the account holder`
ASSUME `an unasked proceeding` IS A `Proceeding`
ASSUME `an unasked death` IS A `The death`

`as family` MEANS `I am a member of the family of someone who has died`
`as executor` MEANS `I am the executor of a will, or want to be granted administration of an estate`
`as beneficiary` MEANS `I am given something by a will`
`as creditor` MEANS `I am owed money by someone who has died`

`a partial will` MEANS `a will that leaves some of their property undisposed of`
`a whole will` MEANS `a will that disposes of all their property`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- s: a husband or wife survived; y: years with a de facto partner; l: lived as the spouse's husband or wife during that
-- time; c, dc: children who survived, dead children leaving issue; p: parents; b, db: brothers and sisters, dead ones
-- leaving children; g: grandparents; u, du: uncles and aunts, dead ones leaving children.
GIVEN s IS A BOOLEAN
      y IS A NUMBER
      l IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A NUMBER
      dc IS A NUMBER
      p IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      db IS A NUMBER
      g IS A NUMBER
      u IS A NUMBER
      du IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The family left behind`
`a family of` s y l c dc p b db g u du MEANS
    `The family left behind` WITH
        `a husband or wife survived`                                           IS s
        `years lived with a de facto partner immediately before the death`     IS y
        `lived as husband or wife of the spouse during any part of that time`  IS l
        `children who survived`                                                IS c
        `children who died first leaving issue who survived`                   IS dc
        `parents who survived`                                                 IS p
        `brothers and sisters who survived`                                    IS b
        `brothers and sisters who died first leaving children who survived`    IS db
        `grandparents who survived`                                            IS g
        `uncles and aunts who survived`                                        IS u
        `uncles and aunts who died first leaving children who survived`        IS du

`Sue in 2060`                              MEANS `a family of` FALSE 0 FALSE 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
`Jake in 2079`                             MEANS `a family of` FALSE 0 FALSE 1 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
`spouse and two children`                  MEANS `a family of` TRUE 0 FALSE 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
`spouse alone`                             MEANS `a family of` TRUE 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
`spouse, both parents and a sister`        MEANS `a family of` TRUE 0 FALSE 0 0 2 1 0 0 0 0
`no relatives`                             MEANS `a family of` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
`de facto of 3 years and two children`     MEANS `a family of` FALSE 3 FALSE 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
`separated spouse and de facto of 3 years` MEANS `a family of` TRUE 3 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0

GIVEN f IS A BOOLEAN
      t IS A BOOLEAN
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The home`
`a home where I lived` f t m MEANS
    `The home` WITH
        `the intestate property includes an interest in the house`                       IS TRUE
        `I ordinarily lived there at the death`                                           IS TRUE
        `it is a tenancy that would end, or the landlord could end, within 2 years`       IS t
        `it is part of a building, farm, hotel or lodging house, or partly not domestic`  IS f
        `months since the first grant of administration`                                  IS m

-- w: left a will; e: the will appoints an executor; i: the executor is an infant; k: willing and competent; r: resides
-- in Western Australia.
GIVEN w IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      i IS A BOOLEAN
      k IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The death`
`a death with` w e i k r MEANS
    `The death` WITH
        `left a will`                                    IS w
        `the will appoints an executor`                  IS e
        `the executor is an infant`                      IS i
        `the executor is willing and competent`          IS k
        `the executor resides in Western Australia`      IS r

`Graham's death in 2052` MEANS `a death with` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`Jake's death in 2079`   MEANS `a death with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a will naming no executor` MEANS `a death with` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Not the figures of the 2023 or 2025 Orders, which the deposit does not give: the baseline's invented sums, to show
-- the input is used.
`hypothetical declared sums` MEANS `Legacy sums` WITH
    `item 2 sum` IS 500000
    `item 3 sum` IS 750000
    `item 3(b)(i) sum` IS 60000
    `item 6 sum` IS 60000

§§ `For a member of the family of someone who has died`

-- s 14(1): only what the will leaves undisposed of is divided. Sue's $900,000 and no will; Graham's will that gives
-- away all of his $500,000 (k084).
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's estate is left for the Table` `as family` 900000 0 EQUALS amount 900000
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's estate is left for the Table` `as family` 500000 600000 EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's estate is left for the Table` `as family` 500000 200000 EQUALS amount 300000

-- Which item: Sue (two children, no partner) item 5; a spouse and two children item 2; a spouse, both parents and a
-- sister item 3; nobody item 11. A will that leaves some property undisposed of still opens the Table.
#ASSERT `Which item of the Table divides my relative's property` `as family` `no will` `Sue in 2060` EQUALS `the answer is` `item 5, issue and no partner`
#ASSERT `Which item of the Table divides my relative's property` `as family` `a partial will` `spouse and two children` EQUALS `the answer is` `item 2, a partner and issue`
#ASSERT `Which item of the Table divides my relative's property` `as family` `no will` `spouse, both parents and a sister` EQUALS `the answer is` `item 3, a partner and a parent or sibling line, no issue`
#ASSERT `Which item of the Table divides my relative's property` `as family` `no will` `no relatives` EQUALS `the answer is` `item 11, nobody, so the Crown`
#ASSERT `Which item of the Table divides my relative's property` `as family` `no will` `spouse alone` EQUALS `the answer is` `item 4, a partner alone`

#ASSERT `Does my relative's property pass to the Crown` `as family` `no will` `no relatives` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does my relative's property pass to the Crown` `as family` `no will` `Sue in 2060` EQUALS no

-- How much do I take. Sue's $900,000: half each, $450,000 (c088, k088). Jake's estate, Ruby alone: all ($638,000,
-- k098). A spouse and two children with $1,072,000: the spouse $472,000 + 1/3 of $600,000 = $672,000; each child 1/2 of
-- $400,000 = $200,000. A spouse, both parents and a sister with $1,005,000: the spouse $705,000 + 1/2 of $300,000 =
-- $855,000; the other half $150,000 exceeds $56,500, so the parents take $56,500 + 1/2 of $93,500 = $103,250, each
-- $51,625; the sister the rest, $46,750.
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's property do I take` `as family` `no will` `a child, or the issue of a child who died first, between them` `Sue in 2060` `the original sums` 900000 EQUALS amount 450000
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's property do I take` `as family` `no will` `a child, or the issue of a child who died first, between them` `Jake in 2079` `the original sums` 638000 EQUALS amount 638000
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's property do I take` `as family` `no will` `the surviving husband or wife` `spouse and two children` `the original sums` 1072000 EQUALS amount 672000
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's property do I take` `as family` `no will` `a child, or the issue of a child who died first, between them` `spouse and two children` `the original sums` 1072000 EQUALS amount 200000
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's property do I take` `as family` `no will` `the surviving husband or wife` `spouse, both parents and a sister` `the original sums` 1005000 EQUALS amount 855000
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's property do I take` `as family` `no will` `a parent` `spouse, both parents and a sister` `the original sums` 1005000 EQUALS amount 51625
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's property do I take` `as family` `no will` `a brother or sister, or the children of one who died first, between them` `spouse, both parents and a sister` `the original sums` 1005000 EQUALS amount 46750
-- A separated spouse and a de facto partner of 3 years, $400,000 and no issue or other kin (item 4): half each (s 15(2)).
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's property do I take` `as family` `no will` `the de facto partner` `separated spouse and de facto of 3 years` `the original sums` 400000 EQUALS amount 200000
#ASSERT `How much of my relative's property do I take` `as family` `a partial will` `a grandparent` `Sue in 2060` `the original sums` 900000 EQUALS amount 0

