#ASSERT `Do we hold my relative's land as tenants in common` `as family` `no will` 1 EQUALS no

-- Fourth Schedule: the spouse of a spouse-and-two-children estate of $1,072,000 takes $672,000, not the whole, so may
-- elect; a farmhouse 14 months after the grant needs both Court orders; a spouse alone takes everything, so may not; a
-- tenancy ending within 2 years is out (cl 1(2)); a child is not the partner.
#ASSERT `May I elect to take my relative's home` `as family` `no will` `the surviving husband or wife` `spouse and two children` `the original sums` 1072000 (`a home where I lived` FALSE FALSE 3) EQUALS `the answer is` `I may elect to take the home towards my share`
#ASSERT `May I elect to take my relative's home` `as family` `no will` `the surviving husband or wife` `spouse and two children` `the original sums` 1072000 (`a home where I lived` TRUE FALSE 14) EQUALS `the answer is` `only if the Court so orders and extends the 12 months`
#ASSERT `May I elect to take my relative's home` `as family` `no will` `the surviving husband or wife` `spouse and two children` `the original sums` 1072000 (`a home where I lived` FALSE FALSE 14) EQUALS `the answer is` `only if the Court extends the 12 months`
#ASSERT `May I elect to take my relative's home` `as family` `no will` `the surviving husband or wife` `spouse alone` `the original sums` 1072000 (`a home where I lived` FALSE FALSE 3) EQUALS `the answer is` `I may not elect`
#ASSERT `May I elect to take my relative's home` `as family` `no will` `the surviving husband or wife` `spouse and two children` `the original sums` 1072000 (`a home where I lived` FALSE TRUE 3) EQUALS `the answer is` `I may not elect`
#ASSERT `May I elect to take my relative's home` `as family` `no will` `a child, or the issue of a child who died first, between them` `spouse and two children` `the original sums` 1072000 (`a home where I lived` FALSE FALSE 3) EQUALS `the answer is` `I may not elect`

-- s 25(1)(b): while Ruby is resident and fit, no outsider (k098); if no one entitled is, or the one cited fails to appear,
-- yes.
#ASSERT `May someone not entitled be granted administration of my relative's estate` `as family` `no will` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May someone not entitled be granted administration of my relative's estate` `as family` `no will` FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May someone not entitled be granted administration of my relative's estate` `as family` `no will` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May someone not entitled be granted administration of my relative's estate` `as family` `no will` FALSE TRUE EQUALS yes

