-- s 71: before a grant, a will is admissible only in criminal proceedings, on an application for a grant, or on its
-- validity; after a grant, in any proceedings.
#ASSERT `Can my relative's will be put in evidence` `as family` `a whole will` `criminal proceedings` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can my relative's will be put in evidence` `as family` `a whole will` `any other proceedings` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can my relative's will be put in evidence` `as family` `a partial will` `any other proceedings` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can my relative's will be put in evidence` `as family` `a partial will` `proceedings on the validity of the will` FALSE EQUALS yes

-- Part V: every charging section is deleted.
#ASSERT `Must my relative's estate pay death duty` `as family` EQUALS no

§§ `For the executor of a will, or a person who wants to be granted administration`

-- Which grant: Graham's will with an adult executor in WA, probate (c087); Jake with no will, letters of administration
-- (k098); a will naming no executor, administration with the will annexed (s 36).
#ASSERT `Which grant must I apply for` `as executor` `Graham's death in 2052` EQUALS `the answer is` `probate`
#ASSERT `Which grant must I apply for` `as executor` `Jake's death in 2079` EQUALS `the answer is` `letters of administration`
#ASSERT `Which grant must I apply for` `as executor` `a will naming no executor` EQUALS `the answer is` `administration with the will annexed`
#ASSERT `Which grant must I apply for` `as executor` (`a death with` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the answer is` `administration with the will annexed`

